'''Liam James Payne''' (29 August 1993 – 16 October 2024) was an English singer and songwriter. He was a member of the pop band [[One Direction]], one of the best-selling boy bands of all time, alongside [[Niall Horan]], [[Zayn Malik]], [[Harry Styles]], and [[Louis Tomlinson]]. Payne twice auditioned as a solo artist on the British television series [[The X Factor&nbsp;(British TV series)|''The X Factor'']] in 2008 and 2010; in the latter, he was invited to join One Direction alongside fellow contestants, placing third and later achieving global success.

Following One Direction's hiatus in 2016, Payne pursued a solo career, signing with [[Republic Records]] in North America.<ref name="republic">{{Cite magazine |last=Kaufman |first=Gil |date=17 October 2016 |title=Liam Payne Joins Ariana Grande & the Weeknd on Republic Records Roster |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop/7542073/liam-payne-signs-to-republic-records-joins-ariana-grande-the-weeknd- |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161017233642/http://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop/7542073/liam-payne-signs-to-republic-records-joins-ariana-grande-the-weeknd- |archive-date=17 October 2016 |access-date=16 August 2018 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> In 2017, he released his debut solo single "[[Strip That Down]]", which reached number three on the [[UK singles chart]] and number ten on the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]]. The song received multi-platinum certifications in both countries. The following year, he released "[[For You (Liam Payne and Rita Ora song)|For You]]", a collaboration with [[Rita Ora]] which became a hit worldwide and received gold or platinum certifications in several countries. His debut and sole solo album, ''[[LP1 (Liam Payne album)|LP1]]'', was released in December 2019. During the first three years of his solo career, Payne sold over 18 million singles, 2.4 million albums, and amassed 3.9 billion streams.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Liam Payne |url=https://www.republicrecords.com/artists/liam-payne |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200922150715/http://www.republicrecords.com/artists/liam-payne |archive-date=22 September 2020 |access-date=17 October 2024 |publisher=[[Republic Records]] }}</ref> In addition to his solo work, Payne produced remixes under the [[pseudonym]]s Big Payno and Payno, remixing tracks for both his group and for singer [[Cheryl (singer)|Cheryl]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=14 October 2014 |title=Listen to 1D's Liam Payne's Remix of Cheryl's new single 'I Don't Care'. |url=https://www.mtv.co.uk/news/zs8o3t/listen-to-1ds-liam-payno-payne-remix-of-cheryls-i-dont-care |access-date=10 January 2016 |publisher=MTV UK}}</ref>

Payne struggled with substance abuse and mental illness throughout his career.<ref name="Henderson" /><ref name="Callahan">{{cite web |last1=Callahan |first1=Chrissy |title=What Liam Payne has shared about his addiction struggle |url=https://www.today.com/health/liam-payne-addiction-rcna175910 |website=Today |access-date=15 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241107004845/https://www.today.com/health/liam-payne-addiction-rcna175910 |archive-date=7 November 2024 |date=17 October 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> On 16 October 2024, he died at the age of 31 after falling from a third-floor balcony at a hotel in [[Buenos Aires]], Argentina, while intoxicated. He had traces of multiple substances in his body.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Spencer-Elliott |first1=Lydia |title=Michael Buerk slams BBC for coverage of ‘drugged up faded boy band singer’ Liam Payne in Radio 4 interview |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/liam-payne-michael-buerk-death-bbc-b2634872.html |access-date=25 July 2026 |work=The Independent |date=24 October 2024}}</ref> Following his death, Payne's track "[[Teardrops (Liam Payne song)|Teardrops]]" debuted on the UK singles chart, alongside the re-entry of 11 of his other works.

==Early life==
Liam James Payne was born at [[New Cross Hospital]] in the [[Heath Town]] district of Wolverhampton<!-- Only name the city per format, no counties etc. --> on 29 August 1993, the son of infant nurse Karen Payne and fitter Geoff Payne. He had two older sisters named Nicola and Ruth.<ref>{{Cite web |date=29 August 2014 |title=ONE DIRECTION STAR Liam Pain Celebrates 21st Birthday in Chicago |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/one-direction-liam-payne-chicago-birthday-tour/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |website=CBS News Chicago |archive-date=7 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220407194456/https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/one-direction-liam-payne-chicago-birthday-tour/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=16 April 2012 |title=Mums of One Direction stars reveal how the boys have grown into music sensations |url=http://www.dailyrecord.co.uk/entertainment/celebrity/mums-of-one-direction-stars-reveal-1119384 |access-date=17 July 2015 |work=Daily Record |archive-date=4 December 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121204235223/http://www.dailyrecord.co.uk/entertainment/celebrity/mums-of-one-direction-stars-reveal-1119384 |url-status=live }}</ref> Payne was born three weeks premature and suffered frequent illnesses. Until the age of four, he had regular tests done in hospital as doctors noticed one of his kidneys was scarred and dysfunctional. In the book ''Dare to Dream: Life as One Direction'', he mentioned that before he was four, "I was always in hospital having tests done but they couldn't find out what was wrong. They discovered that one of my kidneys wasn't working properly and it had scarred. I had to have 32 injections in my arm in the morning and evening to try and make me better."<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/showbiz/a340979/one-directions-liam-payne-i-effectively-died-as-a-baby |last=Davies |first=Rebecca |date=18 September 2011 |title=One Direction's Liam Payne: 'I effectively died as a baby' |publisher=[[Digital Spy]] |accessdate=18 October 2024 |archive-date=11 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231011212707/https://www.digitalspy.com/showbiz/a340979/one-directions-liam-payne-i-effectively-died-as-a-baby/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite book |url=https://archive.org/details/daretodreamlifea0000unse |title=Dare to Dream: Life As One Direction |publication-date=2011 |author=[[One Direction]] |publisher=[[HarperCollins]] |isbn=978-0-00-744439-7 |location=New York |accessdate=22 October 2024}}</ref>

As a student, Payne was heavily involved in sports, particularly cross-country running. Payne joined the [[Wolverhampton & Bilston Athletics Club]] to pursue his running career.

He began taking boxing lessons at the age of 12 amidst bullying from older students in secondary school.<ref>{{Cite news |title=One Direction's Liam Payne: "I Was Devastated After Breaking Up With Danielle Peazer |url=https://www.capitalfm.com/artists/one-direction/news/liam-payne-danielle-peazer-break-up/ |agency=Capital FM |archive-date=21 March 2019 |access-date=16 May 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190321025446/https://www.capitalfm.com/artists/one-direction/news/liam-payne-danielle-peazer-break-up/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Payne completed 11 [[GCSE]]s at St Peter's Collegiate School (now [[St Peter's Collegiate Academy]]) before moving on to study music technology at [[City of Wolverhampton College]].<ref name="auto">{{Cite web |last=Nash |first=Victoria |date=11 September 2010 |title=Liam Payne now sprinting to X Factor success |url=https://www.expressandstar.com/entertainment/2010/09/11/liam-payne-now-sprinting-to-x-factor-success/ |access-date=17 July 2015 |website=Express & Star |archive-date=5 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180705033249/https://www.expressandstar.com/entertainment/2010/09/11/liam-payne-now-sprinting-to-x-factor-success/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Payne was introduced to the world of show business at the age of 12, as a member of the Pink Productions Theatre Company, appearing as Tony Manero from ''[[Saturday Night Fever]]''.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Liam Payne theatre company holds auditions to find their 'next star' |url=http://nativemonster.com/lifestyle/liam-payne-theatre-company-on-look-out-for-next-star |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151222120410/http://nativemonster.com/lifestyle/liam-payne-theatre-company-on-look-out-for-next-star |archive-date=22 December 2015 |access-date=20 October 2015 |publisher=Native Monster}}</ref> Payne had previously performed in front of a crowd of 26,000 during a [[Wolverhampton Wanderers]] football match.<ref name="auto" /><ref>{{Cite news |title=Liam Payne's journey from Bushbury to Big Apple |url=https://www.expressandstar.com/entertainment/music/2012/03/17/liam-paynes-journey-from-bushbury-to-big-apple/ |access-date=17 July 2015 |work=[[Express & Star]] |archive-date=21 March 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190321025445/https://www.expressandstar.com/entertainment/music/2012/03/17/liam-paynes-journey-from-bushbury-to-big-apple/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Career==
===2008–2015: ''The X Factor'' and One Direction===
{{Main|One Direction}}
[[File:Liam Payne Sydney Australia.jpg|thumb|left|180px|Payne performing with One Direction in Sydney, Australia, April 2012]]
Payne auditioned for the fifth series of ''[[The X Factor (British TV series)|The X Factor]]'' in 2008, at 14 years old, in front of judges [[Simon Cowell]], [[Cheryl Cole]], [[Dannii Minogue]] and [[Louis Walsh]]. Payne moved past the first round after performing [[Frank Sinatra]]'s "[[Fly Me to the Moon]]". He was cut at the boot camp stage, but Cowell then changed his mind and asked Payne to return for the judges' houses stage.<ref>{{Cite news |date=6 September 2010 |title=Liam Payne shows he has the X Factor |url=https://www.expressandstar.com/entertainment/2010/09/06/liam-payne-shows-he-has-the-x-factor/ |access-date=26 November 2015 |work=Wolverhampton Express And Star |archive-date=27 November 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151127032352/http://www.expressandstar.com/entertainment/2010/09/06/liam-payne-shows-he-has-the-x-factor/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Payne was cut again during judges' houses, but was encouraged by Cowell to "come back in two years".<ref>{{Cite episode |title=Episode 1 |series=The X Factor (series 5) |series-link=The X Factor (UK) |station=[[ITV (TV network)|ITV]] |date=16 August 2008 |location=London}}</ref>

Payne returned to the show in 2010 for the seventh series, auditioning in front of Cowell, Cole, Walsh and guest judge [[Natalie Imbruglia]]. He sang the [[Michael Bublé]] version of "[[Cry Me a River (1953 song)|Cry Me a River]]".<ref>{{Cite episode |title=Episode 3 |series=The X Factor (series 7) |series-link=The X Factor (UK) |station=[[ITV (TV network)|ITV]] |date=4 September 2010 |location=London}}</ref> He advanced but did not progress to the "Boys" category at judges' houses. During the boot camp stage of the competition, Payne, along with Harry Styles, Niall Horan, Louis Tomlinson, and Zayn Malik, were put together to form a five-piece boy band called One Direction, to compete in the "Groups" category.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kelly |first=Kristy |date=26 July 2011 |title=Nicole Scherzinger: 'I did Simon Cowell a favour with One Direction' |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a331792/nicole-scherzinger-i-did-simon-cowell-a-favour-with-one-direction/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |website=Digital Spy |archive-date=24 September 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150924234216/http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s103/the-x-factor/news/a331792/nicole-scherzinger-i-did-simon-cowell-a-favour-with-one-direction.html |url-status=live }}</ref> The group became the last contestant eliminated on the show.<ref>{{Cite magazine |date=9 April 2012 |title=Exclusive Q&A: Simon Cowell on One Direction's Rise to Stardom |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/exclusive-qa-simon-cowell-on-one-directions-rise-to-stardom-77999/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |magazine=Rolling Stone |archive-date=23 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180723212519/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/exclusive-qa-simon-cowell-on-one-directions-rise-to-stardom-77999/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

In January 2011, One Direction were signed to Simon Cowell's [[Syco Entertainment]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Nicholson |first=Rebecca |title=Also-rans to world's biggest boy band: the rise of One Direction |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2012/nov/17/one-direction-biggest-band-world |access-date=20 October 2015 |work=The Guardian |archive-date=17 October 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171017043302/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2012/nov/17/one-direction-biggest-band-world |url-status=live }}</ref> Their UK number one debut single, "[[What Makes You Beautiful]]", and their debut studio album, ''[[Up All Night (One Direction album)|Up All Night]]'', were released later that year.<ref>{{cite news |last=Jones |first=Alan |date=19 September 2011 |title=What Makes You Beautiful becomes fastest seller of the year |url=http://www.musicweek.com/story.asp?sectioncode=22&storycode=1046622 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120116085928/http://www.musicweek.com/story.asp?sectioncode=22&storycode=1046622 |archive-date=16 January 2012 |access-date=5 January 2012 |work=[[Music Week]] |publisher=Intent Media}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Daniels |first=Colin |date=16 October 2011 |title=One Direction name debut album 'Up All Night', reveal cover |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/music/a345784/one-direction-name-debut-album-up-all-night-reveal-cover/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210309141751/https://www.digitalspy.com/music/a345784/one-direction-name-debut-album-up-all-night-reveal-cover/ |archive-date=9 March 2021 |access-date=9 March 2021 |work=[[Digital Spy]]}}</ref> The album, which contained three songs co-written by Payne, debuted at number one in the United States.<ref name="notes">{{cite AV media notes |title=Up All Night |date=2011 |type=liner notes |publisher=[[Syco Music]], [[Sony Music Entertainment]]}} One Direction</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Caulfield |first=Keith |date=20 March 2012 |title=One Direction Makes History With No. 1 Debut on Billboard 200 |url=https://www.billboard.com/articles/news/499420/one-direction-makes-history-with-no-1-debut-on-billboard-200 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130214140936/http://www.billboard.com/articles/news/499420/one-direction-makes-history-with-no-1-debut-on-billboard-200 |archive-date=14 February 2013 |access-date=29 June 2024 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> All of their next four studio albums—''[[Take Me Home (One Direction album)|Take Me Home]]'' (2012), ''[[Midnight Memories]]'' (2013), ''Four'' (2014) and ''[[Made in the A.M.]]'' (2015)—debuted at number one in the UK.<ref>{{cite news |author=Dan Lane |date=18 November 2012 |title=One Direction score number 1 single and album! |url=https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/one-direction-score-number-1-single-and-album-__2564/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210309011817/https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/one-direction-score-number-1-single-and-album-__2564/ |archive-date=9 March 2021 |access-date=9 March 2021 |publisher=[[Official Charts]]}}

{{cite news |last=Lane |first=Daniel |date=1 December 2013 |title=One Direction score fastest selling album of their career with Midnight Memories |url=https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/one-direction-score-fastest-selling-album-of-their-career-with-midnigh__3580/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210309012044/https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/one-direction-score-fastest-selling-album-of-their-career-with-midnigh__3580/ |archive-date=9 March 2021 |access-date=9 March 2021 |publisher=[[Official Charts]]}}

{{cite web |last=Myers |first=Justin |date=23 November 2014 |title=Four scores One Direction a third consecutive Number 1 album |url=https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/four-scores-one-direction-a-third-consecutive-official-albums-chart-number-1__7285/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210309012455/https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/four-scores-one-direction-a-third-consecutive-official-albums-chart-number-1__7285/ |archive-date=9 March 2021 |access-date=9 March 2021 |publisher=[[Official Charts]]}}

{{cite web |last=Talbot |first=Martin |date=20 November 2015 |title=One Direction vs Justin Bieber: How this week's album chart race was won |url=http://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/one-direction-vs-justin-bieber-how-this-weeks-album-chart-race-was-won__12061/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210309012624/https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/one-direction-vs-justin-bieber-how-this-weeks-album-chart-race-was-won__12061/ |archive-date=9 March 2021 |access-date=20 November 2015 |publisher=[[Official Charts]]}}</ref> ''Midnight Memories'' was the world's best-selling album of 2013,<ref>{{cite web |title=One Direction claim the world's biggest selling album of 2013 |url=https://www.bpi.co.uk/home/one-direction-claim-the-worlds-biggest-selling-album-of-2013.aspx |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140518073935/https://www.bpi.co.uk/home/one-direction-claim-the-worlds-biggest-selling-album-of-2013.aspx |archive-date=18 May 2014 |access-date=30 October 2019 |publisher=The British Recorded Music Industry}}</ref> and its accompanying [[Where We Are Tour (One Direction)|Where We Are Tour]] was the highest-grossing tour of 2014.<ref>{{cite magazine |title=These Were the 10 Highest-Grossing Tours of 2014 |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/hughmcintyre/2015/03/24/these-were-the-10-highest-grossing-tours-of-2014/#673c117c3643 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190718234838/https://www.forbes.com/sites/hughmcintyre/2015/03/24/these-were-the-10-highest-grossing-tours-of-2014/#673c117c3643 |archive-date=18 July 2019 |access-date=20 July 2019 |magazine=[[Forbes]]}}</ref> After the release of ''Four'', One Direction became the only group in the 58-year history of the [[Billboard Hot 200|''Billboard'' 200]] albums chart to have their first four albums debut at number one.<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Caufield |first1=Keith |title=One Direction's 'Four' Makes Historic No. 1 Debut on Billboard 200 Chart |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/one-direction-four-no-1-debut-billboard-200/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141127143625/http://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/chart-beat/6327789/one-direction-four-no-1-debut-billboard-200 |archive-date=27 November 2014 |access-date=20 October 2015 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> The albums spawned a string of successful singles, including "[[Live While We're Young]]", "[[Little Things (One Direction song)|Little Things]]", "[[Best Song Ever]]", "[[Story of My Life (One Direction song)|Story of My Life]]", "[[Drag Me Down]]" and "[[History (One Direction song)|History]]".<ref>{{cite web |date=25 August 2015 |title=One Direction's Official Top 10 Biggest Selling Singles Revealed! |url=http://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/one-direction-s-official-top-10-biggest-selling-singles-revealed-__7226/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150829090736/http://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/one-direction-s-official-top-10-biggest-selling-singles-revealed-__7226/ |archive-date=29 August 2015 |access-date=15 September 2018 |publisher=[[Official Charts]]}}</ref><ref name="1D sales">{{cite magazine |last=Trust |first=Gary |date=19 June 2016 |title=Ask Billboard: One Direction's Career Sales |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/ask-billboard-one-directions-career-sales/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180627151555/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/chart-beat/7408939/ask-billboard-one-directions-career-sales |archive-date=27 June 2018 |access-date=15 September 2018 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Copsey |first=Rob |date=23 July 2020 |title=Ten years of One Direction: 10 chart facts you probably didn't know about one of the UK's most loved boybands |url=https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/ten-years-of-one-direction-10-chart-facts-you-probably-didnt-know-about-one-of-the-uks-most-loved-boybands__30301/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210116044942/https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/ten-years-of-one-direction-10-chart-facts-you-probably-didnt-know-about-one-of-the-uks-most-loved-boybands__30301/ |archive-date=16 January 2021 |access-date=9 March 2021 |publisher=[[Official Charts]]}}</ref> Following the departure of Zayn Malik in March 2015, Payne was tasked with taking over the bulk of Malik's vocals.<ref>{{Cite news |last=McCorimck |first=Neil |title=One Direction, Millennium Stadium Cardiff, review: 'business as usual' |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/music/live-music-reviews/11655547/One-Direction-Millenium-Stadium-Cardiff-review-In-an-ear-battering-competition-between-a-giant-PA-and-female-fandom-Id-say-the-girls-just-about-edged-it.html |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220112/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/music/live-music-reviews/11655547/One-Direction-Millenium-Stadium-Cardiff-review-In-an-ear-battering-competition-between-a-giant-PA-and-female-fandom-Id-say-the-girls-just-about-edged-it.html |archive-date=12 January 2022 |access-date=20 October 2015 |newspaper=[[The Daily Telegraph]]}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

Payne was credited for co-writing more than half of the songs on One Direction's third and fourth albums.<ref name="topearnersandcosongwriters">{{Cite news |last=Corner |first=Lewis |title=One Direction's Liam Payne, Louis Tomlinson named band's top earners |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/music/one-direction-1d-mania/a555301/one-directions-liam-payne-louis-tomlinson-named-bands-top-earners/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |publisher=[[Digital Spy]] |archive-date=7 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220407194456/https://www.digitalspy.com/music/one-direction-1d-mania/a555301/one-directions-liam-payne-louis-tomlinson-named-bands-top-earners/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Liam Payne Now Writing Post-Zayn 1D Songs |url=http://www.inquisitr.com/2008232/liam-payne-now-writing-post-zayn-1d-songs-guess-next-album-title/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181204005658/https://www.inquisitr.com/2008232/liam-payne-now-writing-post-zayn-1d-songs-guess-next-album-title/ |archive-date=4 December 2018 |access-date=20 October 2015 |publisher=Inquisitr}}</ref> Together with Louis Tomlinson, Payne was also the band's top earner.<ref name="topearnersandcosongwriters" /> In 2014, Payne began working as a producer under the monikers "Big Payno" or "Payno", teaming up with fellow producers AfterHrs to remix several tracks including Cheryl's "[[I Don't Care (Cheryl song)|I Don't Care]]" in 2014.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Villa |first=Lucas |title=One Direction's Liam Payne remixes latest singles by his band and Cheryl |url=http://www.axs.com/listen-one-direction-s-liam-payne-remixes-latest-singles-by-his-band-a-24150 |access-date=20 October 2015 |publisher=[[AXS (company)|AXS]] |archive-date=9 April 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190409044617/https://www.axs.com/listen-one-direction-s-liam-payne-remixes-latest-singles-by-his-band-a-24150 |url-status=live}}</ref> Payne was also credited with co-writing Cole's "I Won't Break", off her album ''[[Only Human (Cheryl Cole album)|Only Human]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |title=BBC Radio 1 – Nick Grimshaw – Ten pop collaborations that made us feel entirely unworthy |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/jjvQttqFB7VNRM5PnNH7Yy/ten-pop-collaborations-that-made-us-feel-entirely-unworthy |access-date=16 October 2024 |publisher=BBC |archive-date=11 December 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161211170728/http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/jjvQttqFB7VNRM5PnNH7Yy/ten-pop-collaborations-that-made-us-feel-entirely-unworthy |url-status=live }}</ref> In August 2014, Payne created and became director of Hampton Music Limited, a publishing company under which his solo projects appeared.<ref name="latinpost.com">{{Cite news|last=Minnis|first=Glenn|title=Jennifer Lopez, Liam Payne Working on New Music Together?|url=https://www.latinpost.com/articles/111272/20160125/jennifer-lopez-liam-payne-working-on-new-music-together.htm|work=Latin Post|date=25 January 2016|access-date=22 October 2024|archive-date=26 November 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241126185454/https://www.latinpost.com/articles/111272/20160125/jennifer-lopez-liam-payne-working-on-new-music-together.htm|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Biurher |first=Yurii |title=HAMPTON MUSIC LIMITED – Overview |url=https://www.aihitdata.com/company/01701875/hampton-music-limited/overview |website=aiHit |access-date=6 December 2019 |archive-date=28 August 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230828052742/https://www.aihitdata.com/company/01701875/hampton-music-limited/overview |url-status=live}}</ref> Payne served as one of the directors for the production company One Mode Productions Limited.<ref>{{Cite magazine |date=3 October 2014 |title=Details on One Direction's Secret Financial Investment in 5 Seconds of Summer |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/one-direction-secret-investment-5-seconds-summer/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |magazine=Billboard |archive-date=7 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220407194458/https://www.billboard.com/pro/one-direction-secret-investment-5-seconds-summer/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2015, Payne co-wrote the Irish band [[Hometown (band)|Hometown]]'s single "[[The Night We Met (HomeTown song)|The Night We Met]]".<ref>{{Cite news |last=Martin |first=Rachel |title=Louis Walsh reveals Liam Payne wrote Hometown's new track |url=http://www.goss.ie/2015/10/louis-walsh-reveals-liam-payne-wrote-hometowns-new-track/50007/ |url-status=dead |agency=[[Goss.ie]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151024211202/http://www.goss.ie/2015/10/louis-walsh-reveals-liam-payne-wrote-hometowns-new-track/50007/ |archive-date=24 October 2015 |access-date=22 October 2015}}</ref>

One Direction went on an indefinite hiatus in 2016, after completing promotional activities related to ''Made in the A.M''.<ref name="rolling stone">{{Cite magazine |last=Crowe |first=Cameron |date=18 April 2017 |title=Harry Styles' New Direction |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/feature/harry-styles-new-direction-119432/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180713193059/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/harry-styles-new-direction-119432/ |archive-date=13 July 2018 |access-date=9 July 2017 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Savage |first=Mark |date=14 April 2020 |title=One Direction are speaking about anniversary reunion, Liam Payne says |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-52283104 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210309141113/https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-52283104 |archive-date=9 March 2021 |access-date=9 March 2021 |publisher=BBC News}}</ref> Since their debut, One Direction have sold 70 million records worldwide, including 7.6 million albums and 26 million singles in the US, becoming one of the best-selling boy bands of all time.<ref name="1D sales" /><ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Lipshutz |first1=Jason |last2=Caulfield |first2=Keith |date=25 March 2015 |title=23 Million Songs, 6 Million Albums & More: One Direction With Zayn Malik, By The Numbers |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/one-direction-zayn-malik-by-the-numbers-6509669/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180919224216/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop-shop/6509669/one-direction-zayn-malik-by-the-numbers |archive-date=19 September 2018 |access-date=15 September 2018 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=21 July 2020 |title=One Direction: Ten years of 1D, but is a reunion on the way? |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/newsround/53447792 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201001160423/https://www.bbc.co.uk/newsround/53447792 |archive-date=1 October 2020 |access-date=1 October 2020 |work=[[BBC]]}}</ref> The group amassed numerous accolades, including seven [[Brit Awards]],<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Weatherby |first=Taylor |date=22 February 2017 |title=One Direction Beats Out Zayn Malik for Video of the Year at 2017 Brit Awards |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/one-direction-zayn-malik-video-of-the-year-2017-brit-awards-7701365/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180825022717/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop/7701365/one-direction-zayn-malik-video-of-the-year-2017-brit-awards |archive-date=25 August 2018 |access-date=24 August 2018 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> seven [[American Music Awards]],<ref>{{cite web |title=Winners Database |url=https://www.theamas.com/winners-database/?winnerKeyword=one+direction&winnerYear=&winnerCategory= |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181106023032/https://www.theamas.com/winners-database/?winnerKeyword=one+direction&winnerYear=&winnerCategory= |archive-date=6 November 2018 |access-date=24 August 2018 |website=[[American Music Awards]] |publisher=[[Dick Clark Productions]]}}</ref> six [[Billboard Music Award|''Billboard'' Music Awards]],<ref>{{cite news |title=Winners Database |url=https://www.billboardmusicawards.com/winners-database/?winnerKeyword=one+direction&winnerYear=&winnerCategory= |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180913075843/https://www.billboardmusicawards.com/winners-database/?winnerKeyword=one+direction&winnerYear=&winnerCategory= |archive-date=13 September 2018 |access-date=24 August 2018 |website=[[Billboard Music Award]]s |publisher=[[Dick Clark Productions]]}}</ref> and four [[MTV Video Music Awards]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Vena |first=Jocelyn |date=25 August 2013 |title=One Direction: Eight Million Votes Prove The Boys Own 'Song Of The Summer' |url=http://www.mtv.com/news/1713022/one-direction-vma-2013-song-of-the-summer/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180825002551/http://www.mtv.com/news/1713022/one-direction-vma-2013-song-of-the-summer/ |archive-date=25 August 2018 |access-date=24 August 2018 |website=[[MTV News]]}}</ref>

===2016–2018: Solo debut and ''First Time''===
In 2015, Payne began working on solo material.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Juicy J made seven songs with Liam Payne: 'We are working on a lot of different things' |url=http://www.pressparty.com/pg/newsdesk/londonnewsdesk/view/121633/ |access-date=20 October 2015 |publisher=Pressparty.com |archive-date=28 August 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230828052730/http://www.pressparty.com/pg/newsdesk/londonnewsdesk/view/121633/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=One Direction's Liam Payne records 'dance' track with Miguel |url=https://www.nme.com/news/one-direction/72221 |access-date=20 October 2015 |work=NME |archive-date=11 October 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151011033350/http://www.nme.com/news/one-direction/72221 |url-status=live }}</ref> In early 2016, Payne featured on a track titled "You" by [[Wiz Khalifa]] and Juicy J; the track was a leak from an unreleased mixtape.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Orcutt |first=KC |date=20 April 2016 |title=Wiz Khalifa and Juicy J Brought A Member Of One Direction into The Hip Hop Game |url=https://www.bet.com/article/16l6l2/boy-band-crooner-has-wiz-khalifa-and-juicy-j-to-thank |access-date=7 April 2022 |archive-date=28 August 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230828052729/https://www.bet.com/article/16l6l2/boy-band-crooner-has-wiz-khalifa-and-juicy-j-to-thank |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Greenwald |first=Morgan |date=20 April 2016 |title=Liam Payne Says 'Leaked' Juicy J & Wiz Khalifa Song Is Just a Demo: 'I Do Not Have a Single' |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/liam-payne-juicy-j-wiz-khalifa-leak-demo-7340846/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |archive-date=7 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220407194435/https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/liam-payne-juicy-j-wiz-khalifa-leak-demo-7340846/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In October 2016, it was announced that Payne had signed a recording contract with Republic Records.<ref name="republic" /> His debut solo single ''Strip That Down'', featuring [[Quavo]] and co-written with [[Ed Sheeran]] and [[Steve Mac]], was released on 19 May 2017.<ref name="firstsingle">{{Cite magazine |date=11 May 2017 |title=Liam Payne Officially Announces First Solo Single, 'Strip That Down,' Featuring Quavo |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/liam-payne-new-single-strip-that-down-release-date-7792797/ |access-date=7 April 2022 |magazine=Billboard |archive-date=7 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220407194455/https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/liam-payne-new-single-strip-that-down-release-date-7792797/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The song was a commercial success, reaching number ten on the
US ''Billboard'' Hot 100 and number three on the UK Singles Chart. "Strip That Down" was certified double platinum in the United Kingdom and 3× platinum in the United States.<ref>{{Cite certification|region=United Kingdom|type=single|award=Platinum|number=2|certyear=2020|access-date=9 June 2020|artist=Liam Payne ft Quavo|title=Strip That Down|id=14363-4426-1}}</ref><ref>{{Cite certification|region=United States|type=single|award=Platinum|number=3|certyear=2018|access-date=7 June 2018|artist=Liam Payne|title=Strip That Down}}</ref> Payne followed up this release with two UK top 30 singles: "[[Get Low (Zedd and Liam Payne song)|Get Low]]", a collaboration with [[Zedd]] which was certified silver, and "[[Bedroom Floor]]", which was certified gold.<ref>{{Cite certification|region=United Kingdom|type=single|award=Silver|artist=Zedd & Liam Payne|title=Get Low|certyear=2018|accessdate=12 January 2018|id=13861-4575-1}}</ref><ref>{{Cite certification|region=United Kingdom|award=Gold|type=single|artist=Liam Payne|title=Bedroom Floor|certyear=2024|access-date=8 March 2024|id=14765-4582-1}}</ref>

In January 2018, Payne collaborated with Rita Ora on "For You", released as a single from the soundtrack of the film ''[[Fifty Shades Freed (film)|Fifty Shades Freed]]''.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Davis |first=Jennifer |date=3 January 2018 |title=Rita Ora and Liam Payne's Fifty Shades Collab Will Be Your First Favorite Song of 2018 |url=http://www.instyle.com/news/rita-ora-liam-payne-fifty-shades-freed-song-for-you |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180124064939/http://www.instyle.com/news/rita-ora-liam-payne-fifty-shades-freed-song-for-you |archive-date=24 January 2018 |access-date=11 February 2018 |work=[[InStyle]]}}</ref> The song was a commercial success worldwide, peaking within the top ten of several countries. "For You" was certified diamond in Brazil, platinum in the United Kingdom, and received gold or platinum certifications in thirteen further countries.<ref>Certifications for "For You"
